  "caveats": [
    "Inauguration Day (20 January, every fourth year) is a legal public holiday under 5 U.S.C. 6103(c) but only for federal employees in the Washington DC area. In 2025 it fell on the same day as Martin Luther King Jr. Day, so it changes nothing here. It is recorded on that entry rather than as a separate row.",
    "21 CFR 803.3(y) says 'Federal holidays' without qualification. This file takes that to mean the days on OPM's federal-holiday table, observed."
  ],
